\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Setting and compared constructions. With labels, unlabeled records and the predictor fixed, three intervals are built from the same data: the labeled-only interval, PPI++ (scalar weight on $\hat  Y$), and recalibrated PPI (cross-fitted $g(\hat  Y)$ as an additional control variate, with a fallback to PPI++). Each is scored by empirical coverage and by the width ratio to PPI++; the achievable narrowing is bounded by the drop from $\mathrm  {Var}(Y-\lambda \hat  Y)$ to the residual variance of the best $g$.}}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Setting and compared constructions. With labels, unlabeled records and the predictor fixed, three intervals are built from the same data: the labeled-only interval, PPI++ (scalar weight on $\Yhat $), and recalibrated PPI (cross-fitted $g(\Yhat )$ as an additional control variate, with a fallback to PPI++). Each is scored by empirical coverage and by the width ratio to PPI++; the achievable narrowing is bounded by the drop from $\Var (Y-\lambda \Yhat )$ to the residual variance of the best $g$}{figure.caption.2}{}}
